    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d674">

                <pb facs="0653" n="1387" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1387"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-12-12"><hi rendition="#italic">December 12, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received Dec. 27.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 719.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose herewith a letter from Rev. Mr.
                    Saunders, dated Aintab, the 27th instant, which gives the first satisfactory
                    account of the massacre at Aintab. The writer is well known to me, and is a
                    brave and worthy missionary. I inclose a copy of my note of this date to the
                    Porte expressive of my appreciation of the conduct of Turkish officers and
                    soldiers in protecting Americans and their property during the massacre. The
                    noble conduct in protecting Americans of Hadji Hasseyn Agha and Mehmed Agha, of
                    the Hiak Baba Mahale in Aintab, saved our people, and I concur with Mr. Saunders
                    in the desire that they shall receive some appropriate recognition of their
                    noble conduct from our Government.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>




                <xi:include href="d674-a1.xml" xpointer="d674-a1"/>
